  "ownership_contract": [
    "Caller owns successfully constructed target slots, including the completed prefix after panic.",
    "Successful callback count can record initialized prefix length; the helper itself does not catch or alter panic payloads.",
    "Caller must eventually move out or drop exactly the initialized slots; MaybeUninit prevents implicit partial cleanup.",
    "Failing slot and suffix are untouched; previously initialized destination payloads are not implicitly destroyed."
  ],
  "remaining_limits": [
    "This binds the protected raw target/source/count helper, not the receiver copy constructor or its allocation-failure leak behavior.",
    "Overlapping placement construction, retained raw aliases, conflicting references and callback reentry are excluded.",
    "Nonempty zero-sized Rust T is rejected; native C++ has no sizeof(T)==0 class domain.",
    "Callbacks return values that move into target storage; address-sensitive/self-referential constructors and partially written failing-slot byte representations are not modeled. Only successfully constructed native objects are observed.",
    "Forced alternate U template-policy selection and native object allocator hooks remain open.",
    "Rust panic preserves the tested construction prefix and payload, not C++ ABI exception mechanics.",
    "Public Assign/CopyValues overlapping-wrapper protocols and shared writable const aliases remain open."
  ],
